\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The R2D2 prior as a variance budget: a Beta prior on \(R^2\) --- together with the residual scale \(\mitsigma \) --- opens a global explained variance \(\mittau ^2\); a flat Dirichlet splits it into per-predictor weights \(\mitphi _j\); and each slice \(\mitlambda _j^2 = \mittau ^2\mitphi _j\) becomes the prior variance of coefficient \(\mitbeta _j\). Dashed nodes are deterministic transforms.}}{1}{figure.caption.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig-r2d2}{{1}{1}{The R2D2 prior as a variance budget: a Beta prior on \(R^2\) --- together with the residual scale \(\sigma \) --- opens a global explained variance \(\tau ^2\); a flat Dirichlet splits it into per-predictor weights \(\phi _j\); and each slice \(\lambda _j^2 = \tau ^2\phi _j\) becomes the prior variance of coefficient \(\beta _j\). Dashed nodes are deterministic transforms}{figure.caption.2}{}}
